---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero from '~/components/widgets/Hero.astro';
import Features from '~/components/widgets/Features.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <Hero>
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Privacy <span class="text-accent dark:text-white">Policy</span>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      <span class="text-lg"> Last updated: September 11, 2026 </span>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <!-- Privacy Content -->
  <section class="px-4 py-16 mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <div class="p-6 bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 mb-8">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-100 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🛡️</span> Our Architectural Privacy Guarantee
        </h3>
        <p class="text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-200 text-base leading-relaxed mb-2">
          <strong>123 ToDo is engineered with privacy as an architectural constraint, not just a policy promise.</strong
          >
        </p>
        <p class="text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-0">
          Your tasks, notes, timestamps, photos, and personal information are processed client-side and stored locally
          on your device by default. We do not collect, view, sell, or profile your personal data. Optional cloud
          synchronization uses military-grade AES-256-GCM zero-knowledge encryption where only you hold the decryption
          key.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8">Last Updated: September 11, 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Introduction & Data Controller</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Unforgettable Management Ltd</strong> ("we," "us," or "our"), as the Data
        Controller, handles information when you access or use 123 ToDo via our website (<a
          href="https://www.123todo.com"
          class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">123todo.com</a
        >), web application (<a href="https://app.123todo.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">app.123todo.com</a
        >), or Progressive Web App (PWA) (collectively, the "Service").
      </p>
      <p>
        Unlike conventional SaaS productivity applications that ingest, index, and store your life's schedule on
        centralized cloud databases, 123 ToDo is built as a <strong>local-first, client-side web application</strong>.
        This document explains the precise technical mechanisms used to protect your privacy across all application
        features.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Technical Architecture & Data Storage Breakdown</h2>

      <h3>A. Core Task, Note & Preference Data (Local Storage)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Storage Engines:</strong> Your task titles, detailed notes, creation timestamps, completion timestamps,
          subtasks, project assignments, and UI preferences (such as light/dark mode, date formats, task character limits,
          and swipe gesture bindings) are stored exclusively within your web browser's local databases (primarily <strong
            >IndexedDB</strong
          > and <strong>LocalStorage</strong>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Domain Isolation:</strong> Web browsers enforce strict same-origin security policies. Your 123 ToDo data
          cannot be inspected or read by any other website or domain.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero Server Transmission:</strong> Under standard operation, your unencrypted task and note data is never
          transmitted to, routed through, or stored on our servers.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>B. Photo Attachments (Local Client Storage)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>In-Browser Processing:</strong> When you snap a picture with your device camera or attach an image from
          your library, the image file is processed and compressed client-side (using an in-memory HTML5 Canvas element)
          directly within your browser.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>IndexedDB Persistence:</strong> Compressed photos are stored locally in your browser's IndexedDB. They
          are not uploaded to any central media server.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Encrypted Sync Payload:</strong> If you enable optional cloud sync, attached photos are encrypted client-side
          alongside your task data before transmission.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>C. Voice Dictation ("Talk" Feature)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Native Browser Web Speech API:</strong> The "Talk" dictation feature operates using your browser's native
          W3C Web Speech API (such as <code>webkitSpeechRecognition</code> or <code>SpeechRecognition</code>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero 123 ToDo Audio Handling:</strong> 123 ToDo does not run audio servers, audio streaming gateways, or
          speech-to-text transcription servers. Voice audio captured during dictation is handled directly by your browser
          engine or operating system (e.g., Apple Speech Recognition on iOS/macOS, or Google Speech Services on Chrome/Android)
          subject to your device's platform privacy settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Live Text Append Only:</strong> 123 ToDo only receives the resulting finalized text string emitted by your
          browser, which is inserted directly into your local task title or notes field.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>D. Automated Local Shadow Backups</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          To safeguard against accidental user edits, 123 ToDo automatically creates localized daily snapshot backups.
        </li>
        <li>
          These shadow snapshots reside exclusively in an isolated, protected IndexedDB store within your own browser on
          your device, and are never transmitted across the network.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>E. Actionable Links (Telephone & Email)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Telephone Links (<code>tel:</code>):</strong> Clicking a detected phone number hands the number directly
          to your device's native phone dialer. No telephony logs are recorded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email Links (<code>mailto:</code> / Webmail):</strong> Clicking an email address opens your operating system's
          default email client or routes to your configured webmail provider (e.g., Gmail, Outlook, or Yahoo Mail) in a new
          browser tab. No email metadata or drafts are intercepted or stored by 123 ToDo.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Optional Multi-Cloud Sync — Zero-Knowledge Cryptography</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose to sync your tasks and notes across multiple devices, 123 ToDo provides optional integration with
        Cloudflare Workers KV, Google Drive, or custom WebDAV servers.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>End-to-End Zero-Knowledge Encryption (E2EE):</strong> All synchronization payloads are encrypted on your
          device prior to leaving your browser using authenticated <strong>AES-256-GCM</strong> (Advanced Encryption Standard
          with Galois/Counter Mode).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cryptographic Key Derivation:</strong> Your encryption key is derived locally in your browser using <strong
            >PBKDF2</strong
          >
          (Password-Based Key Derivation Function 2) with SHA-256, utilizing a cryptographically random salt and a high iteration
          count (100,000+ rounds).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero Server Visibility:</strong> Your master encryption passphrase is never transmitted across the network,
          never sent to our servers, and never saved in unencrypted cloud files. The storage endpoints (whether Cloudflare,
          Google Drive, or WebDAV) only ever receive and store opaque, undecryptable ciphertext blobs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google OAuth 2.0:</strong> If you use Google Drive Sync, authentication is handled directly through Google
          Identity Services. We only request scoped permission to read and write a dedicated application file in your personal
          Google Drive. We never receive or store your Google password.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Information We Do NOT Collect</h2>
      <p>To provide absolute clarity, 123 ToDo does NOT collect, harvest, monitor, or monetize any of the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No Personal Identifiers:</strong> No names, email addresses, phone numbers, or physical addresses are required
          to use the app.
        </li>
        <li><strong>No Account Credentials:</strong> No master passwords, usernames, or security questions.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Task Content or Photos:</strong> We cannot view what you write, plan, schedule, or photograph.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Third-Party Analytics Trackers:</strong> We do not embed Google Analytics, Mixpanel, Amplitude, Hotjar,
          or any behavioral tracking SDKs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Advertising Trackers or Pixels:</strong> No Meta Pixel, TikTok Pixel, Google Ads remarketing tags, or
          third-party ad networks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Browser Fingerprinting:</strong> We do not collect canvas hashes, audio context signatures, font lists,
          or battery status.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Sale of Data:</strong> We have never sold, and will never sell, lease, or monetize user data.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Cookies & Local Browser Storage</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>123 ToDo does not use tracking cookies or marketing cookies.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not set first-party tracking cookies or permit third-party advertising cookies. As detailed above, the
        application utilizes modern HTML5 client storage mechanisms (IndexedDB, LocalStorage, and Cache Storage via
        Service Workers) strictly for essential functionality: persisting your tasks locally, remembering your UI theme,
        and enabling offline Progressive Web App (PWA) operation without internet connectivity.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Edge CDN Infrastructure & Ephemeral Logs</h2>
      <p>
        When you load the static files of 123 ToDo (HTML, JavaScript, CSS, and SVG icons), requests are routed through <strong
          >Cloudflare</strong
        >'s global content delivery network (CDN).
      </p>
      <p>
        Like all web infrastructure, Cloudflare edge nodes process standard, transient HTTP request headers (including
        your IP address and user-agent) solely for the purposes of content caching, SSL termination, and mitigating
        automated DDoS attacks. These technical network logs are managed by Cloudflare in accordance with their strict
        privacy standards, are retained only ephemerally for security analysis, and are never correlated with user
        activity or task contents.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Future Monetisation & Payment Information Disclosures</h2>
      <p>
        While 123 ToDo is currently free to access, Unforgettable Management Ltd reserves the right to introduce
        optional paid features, subscriptions, or commercial tiers in the future.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Third-Party Payment Gateways:</strong> In the event that commercial services, subscription tiers, or paid
        licenses are introduced:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          All financial transactions and payment processing will be handled entirely by established, certified <strong
            >PCI-DSS Level 1 compliant third-party payment processors</strong
          > (such as Stripe, Lemon Squeezy, or official platform app stores).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero Financial Data Retention:</strong> Unforgettable Management Ltd will never collect, process, or store
          your raw credit card numbers, debit card details, CVV codes, or bank account credentials on our servers.
        </li>
        <li>
          Any transition to paid services will be accompanied by updated commercial disclosures, and users will always
          retain the free right to export all their existing data prior to changes taking effect.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Your Rights Under GDPR, UK GDPR, and CCPA / CPRA</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your location, you hold statutory rights under data protection legislation, including the <strong
          >General Data Protection Regulation (EU GDPR)</strong
        >, the <strong>UK Data Protection Act 2018 (UK GDPR)</strong>, and the <strong
          >California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA)</strong
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because 123 ToDo operates on a decentralized, local-first architecture, your rights are fulfilled
        instantaneously through self-service app features:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Access & Portability:</strong> You can access your complete data at any second directly within
          the interface, or click
          <strong>Settings ⚙️ ➔ Import / Export Data ➔ Export Backup</strong> to instantly generate and download a complete,
          unencumbered JSON copy of your entire dataset.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Erasure ("Right to Be Forgotten"):</strong> You can permanently erase all local tasks, notes,
          and photos at any time by clearing your browser's site data / cache, or by tapping "Clear All Data" in settings.
          For cloud sync, you can delete your sync file or revoke access directly with your provider.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> You can edit, modify, or correct any task, note, or timestamp directly
          within the app.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> We do not discriminate against any user for exercising their privacy
          rights.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. Children's Online Privacy Protection (COPPA)</h2>
      <p>
        123 ToDo does not knowingly collect, solicit, or maintain personal information from children under the age of 13
        (or under 16 in the European Union). Because the application collects no personal identifiers or account
        registrations from any user, it is fundamentally safe for users of all ages.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Data Security & User Responsibilities</h2>
      <p>
        While we implement strict cryptographic zero-knowledge standards for cloud sync, the security of your local data
        depends on your device security:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Device Passcodes & Biometrics:</strong> Ensure your phone, tablet, or computer is protected by a strong
          passcode, PIN, or biometric lock (Face ID, Touch ID, fingerprint), preventing unauthorized physical access to your
          browser's local databases.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Shared Computers:</strong> If using a shared or public computer, always use a separate OS user profile
          or clear your browser data upon completion.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Passphrase Stewardship:</strong> Because cloud sync encryption keys are derived mathematically from your
          passphrase, you are solely responsible for safeguarding your passphrase. If lost, your synced data cannot be decrypted
          by anyone.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect new features, operational enhancements, or legal
        requirements. Any modifications will be published directly to this page with an updated "Last Updated" date. We
        encourage you to review this policy periodically.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our foundational architectural commitment will remain unchanging: <strong
          >We will never sell your data, deploy user tracking scripts, or compromise our local-first, zero-knowledge
          privacy architecture.</strong
        >
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact & Data Protection Inquiries</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions, feedback, or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy or our privacy practices, please
        contact us:
      </p>
      <div class="p-6 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/60 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 my-4">
        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 mb-1">Unforgettable Management Ltd</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-1">Data Controller • Registered in England and Wales</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-1">
          Web: <a href="https://www.123todo.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">www.123todo.com</a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-0">
          UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) Jurisdiction
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Privacy Features Grid -->
  <Features
    id="privacy-features"
    tagline="Privacy by Design"
    title="How We Protect Your Digital Privacy"
    subtitle="Privacy isn't a marketing claim — it's our core software architecture"
    items={[
      {
        title: 'Local-First Storage',
        description:
          'All tasks, notes, and photos reside on your device in IndexedDB. Zero unencrypted data on our servers.',
        icon: 'tabler:database',
      },
      {
        title: 'Zero-Knowledge Encryption',
        description: 'Cloud sync uses client-side AES-256-GCM encryption. Even storage hosts cannot read your data.',
        icon: 'tabler:lock',
      },
      {
        title: 'Zero Tracking & No Cookies',
        description: 'No Google Analytics, no Meta pixels, no tracking cookies, and no browser fingerprinting. Ever.',
        icon: 'tabler:eye-off',
      },
      {
        title: 'No Accounts Required',
        description: 'No email sign-ups, no passwords to remember, no personal profiling, and no identity tracking.',
        icon: 'tabler:user-off',
      },
      {
        title: 'Private Voice Dictation',
        description:
          'Speech recognition runs through your native browser engine. We never stream or record your voice.',
        icon: 'tabler:microphone',
      },
      {
        title: 'Instant 1-Click Portability',
        description: 'Export all your data anytime as an open JSON file. Zero data lock-in, full user sovereignty.',
        icon: 'tabler:shield-check',
      },
    ]}
  />
</Layout>
